Fixed TCP SYN host checks reporting online hosts as offline on Windows (SYN retransmissions after a RST
delayed "connection refused" past the timeout) and on macOS (ECONNREFUSED is 61, not 111).
Fixed WSL 2 not being detected as WSL, and MAC lookups via ``arp.exe`` on Windows and WSL returning the
first MAC in the ARP table instead of the one for the requested IP. On Linux, looking up the MAC for
an IP like ``192.0.2.1`` could return the MAC of ``192.0.2.10`` if that came first in ``/proc/net/arp``.
Text files are now always read and written as UTF-8 instead of the Windows code page, and redirected console output on Windows escapes characters it can't encode
instead of crashing.
UDP fingerprinting on Windows no longer raises an error when the port is closed (Windows reports
ICMP "port unreachable" as a connection reset), and treats it as no response, like Linux and macOS.
